# Local-only install copies and convenience symlinks created by an agent
# installer (or manually) for this developer's own machine. None of this is
# the real skill catalogue.
#
# The real, canonical, git-tracked skill source always lives at
# skills/<category>/<name>/ (for example skills/planning/plan-review/), and
# the real, canonical, git-tracked host wrappers always live at
# agents/<persona>/ (for example agents/plan-builder/). Neither of those
# paths is listed below, and this file must never gain a rule that matches
# them.
#
# /.agents/ and /.claude/skills/ are directories some tools install skills
# into; /agent/ is an older, singular-named install target from before this
# layout; /skills/<name> below (flat, no <category>/ in the path) are
# per-skill convenience symlinks some installs create at the top level so a
# skill can be reached without knowing its category. All of it is
# reconstructible by re-running an installer, none of it has ever been
# committed to this repository, and hiding it here only keeps `git status`
# from showing local noise.
/.agents/
/agent/
/skills-lock.json
/.claude/skills/
/skills/ai-audit
/skills/ai-review
/skills/conventions-codifier
/skills/create-agent
/skills/doc-cleanup
/skills/issue-refiner
/skills/plan-review
/skills/plan-writer
/skills/pr-description
/skills/review-response
/skills/secret-and-privacy-sweep
/skills/skill-writer
/skills/tech-writing
/skills/ui-engineering
